Update the container status that a remote status names.

handleContainersUpdate and handleInitContainersUpdate looked up each remote
status by name, appended it when no in-cluster status matched, and kept the
index at 0. The update then landed on the first container's status: it was
marked Ready and Running for a container that never started, and a terminated
remote status panicked on the first entry's nil Terminated state.

trackedContainerStatus returns the in-cluster entry to update. A name that
belongs to the pod spec but has no status yet is appended and updated at its
own index (len-1). A name outside the pod spec gets a detached copy, so it
still counts toward the pod phase as before but never adds a status the pod
spec cannot account for.

Depends on 0001 for the shared test fixtures.

Upstream status: reported to interlink-hq/interLink in a drafted issue, not
yet filed (see readme).

